# Security & Authentication Patterns

## Authentication & Authorization
- Use Clerk with JWT verification
- Always use `get_effective_user` dependency
- Validate user ownership before data access
- Filter all queries by user_id

## Data Protection
- Validate all inputs with Pydantic schemas
- Sanitize data, validate files (type, size)
- HTML escape user content
- Never trust user inputs

## API Security
- CORS for production, rate limiting per endpoint
- Validate request parameters, use HTTPS
- Log suspicious requests

## Database Security
- Use SQLAlchemy ORM (no raw SQL)
- Always filter by user_id, audit operations

## Error Handling
- Generic error messages for users
- Log detailed errors server-side only
- Don't expose stack traces or system info

## Best Practices
- Never commit secrets, use env vars
- Regular security updates, HTTPS only
